<div class="details-container">
    <div class="bio-block details-block">
        <div class="bio-content content-holder">
        <div class="title-holder">
            <h3>Biography</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="description-holder">
            <p>
                Yechiel Kalmenson (aka Rabbi On Rails) found his way to software development through an unconventional path. Born in Brooklyn and trained as a rabbi in Israel, he spent his early career teaching—a role that taught him how to break down complex concepts and guide others through challenging problems.
            </p>
            <p>
                After discovering that debugging code scratched the same intellectual itch as Talmudic analysis, he made the leap into web development. The transition from ancient texts to modern frameworks proved surprisingly natural.
            </p>
            <p>
                He now lives in New Jersey with his family, where he works as 
                <% if current_title.present? %>
                  <%= [current_title.downcase, current_employer].compact.join(' at ') %>
                <% else %>
                  a software engineer
                <% end %>. 
                A passionate programmer and writer, Yechiel is the published author of <a href="<%= SocialLinks.torah_tech %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>Torah && Tech</em></a> and actively maintains his technical blog <a href="<%= blog_path %>"><em>Rabbi on Rails</em></a>. When he's not coding or serving on the RubyConf Program Committee, you'll likely find him writing about the intersection of software and ethics, explaining why good code and good teaching have more in common than most people think.
            </p>
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="education-block details-block">
        <div class="education-content content-holder">
        <div class="title-holder">
            <h3>Education</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="description-holder">
            <h4>Flatiron School</h4>
            <h5>Web Development</h5><br>
            <h4>United Lubavitch Yeshivah</h4>
            <h5>Rabbinical Studies</h5>
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="experience-block details-block">
        <%# 
        REMINDER: When updating experience below, also update:
